			},
			"date": "2023-04-19T23:50:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@rich_harris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rich_harris</span></a></span> nobody is calling for abolishment of anything. Ppl do point out tradeoffs in dev velocity, determinism in build artifacts,  debugging being more difficult, etc. It's a reduction to the absurd to say abolish when the discussion is more about starting from simplest things that could work and opting into complexity as required.</p>",
