			"date": "2023-04-20T07:38:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@keithamus\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>keithamus</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@rich_harris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rich_harris</span></a></span> Think he chose a bad example there. It isn't just a markdown renderer presumably but needs to do lookups/resolution of referenced issues etc. We have a similar component, we do it clientside like he's suggesting and it *quickly* gets complex...</p>",
