			"date": "2023-04-20T11:42:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@rich_harris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rich_harris</span></a></span> It’s good to see captions on these things, but not when they’re still in autogenerated craption form. It would be better if someone had a ticket to sit an edit them between being generated and going public. Here’s one of my favourite examples. </p><p>Rich, you’d better get that wordal plane on the spurtleclean in the next release, or you’re in big trouble, mate.</p><p><a href=\"https://home.social/tags/accessibility\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>accessibility</span></a> <a href=\"https://home.social/tags/captions\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>captions</span></a> <a href=\"https://home.social/tags/craptions\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>craptions</span></a> <a href=\"https://home.social/tags/wordalPlane\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>wordalPlane</span></a> <a href=\"https://home.social/tags/spurtleclean\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>spurtleclean</span></a></p>",
